From: GKI maintainers <gki-builder@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] susfs: define ratelimited log macros when logging is disabled

Upstream commit 41da83f3 ("kernel: ratelimit on logging sus selinux type and
rule") introduced SUSFS_LOGI_RL and SUSFS_LOGE_RL inside the
CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS_ENABLE_LOG branch, but omitted empty macro fallbacks in the
#else branch. When CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS_ENABLE_LOG is unset (production build),
calls to SUSFS_LOGI_RL in susfs_add_sus_type() and
susfs_add_sus_avd_allowed_by_type() fail with
-Werror,-Wimplicit-function-declaration. Define both as empty macros in the
#else branch.

diff --git a/fs/susfs.c b/fs/susfs.c
--- a/fs/susfs.c
+++ b/fs/susfs.c
@@ -45,4 +45,6 @@
 #else
 #define SUSFS_LOGI(fmt, ...) 
 #define SUSFS_LOGE(fmt, ...) 
+#define SUSFS_LOGI_RL(fmt, ...) 
+#define SUSFS_LOGE_RL(fmt, ...) 
 #endif
